  "id": "COMPOUND:17643 - PROTEIN:6335",
  "verbalization": "Hydroxyanthecotulide is implicated in the regulation of Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7 through two distinct pathways. The first pathway links Hydroxyanthecotulide to Regulator of G-protein signaling 12, which in turn targets a complex polyketide compound. This compound then directly interacts with Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7, suggesting a potential role in modulating its activity. The second pathway connects Hydroxyanthecotulide to ADP-ribosylation factor-like protein 3, which targets another compound that also ultimately binds to Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7. Both pathways highlight a potential mechanism by which Hydroxyanthecotulide may influence the function of this protein, possibly through indirect interactions that involve complex metabolic or signaling cascades. The evidence suggests that Hydroxyanthecotulide may act as a regulator of Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7 via multiple, interconnected molecular pathways, emphasizing the importance of these interactions in drug resistance mechanisms.",
